# Social Structure in Organizations

Social structure refers to the communication patterns, decision-making processes, and relational norms within an organization. Sinek identifies it as one of three essential elements for successful leader-led organizations, alongside physical space and shared purpose.

## Key Ideas
- How information flows determines how trust builds
- Decision-making processes should be transparent and inclusive
- Social structures either enable or inhibit collaboration
- Strong social structures create feedback loops that reinforce belonging

## Connection to Team Dynamics
This concept connects to [[building-a-cohesive-team]] and [[the-five-dysfunctions-of-a-team]], both of which emphasize that healthy communication and trust are prerequisites for high performance.

